1. mtg-table (jalirkan/mtg-table)
---------------------------------

    Source:   https://github.com/jalirkan/mtg-table
    Licence:  GNU General Public License v3.0 or later (GPL-3.0-or-later)
    Copyright (C) 2026 the mtg-table authors

ForgeCoach reads the frame logs mtg-table writes (its docs/protocol.md).
src/protocol.ts is copied verbatim from mtg-table's web/src/protocol.ts and
keeps its original copyright and licence header. The sample logs in
public/samples/ are recordings from mtg-table's fixture corpus, gzipped.
In play mode ForgeCoach takes the player's seat on mtg-table's bridge; the play
keyboard (src/ui/play/playKeys.ts) is adapted from mtg-table's web/src/keys.ts.
The play board's stack panel and its lines (src/ui/StackPanel.tsx,
src/ui/stackModel.ts, src/ui/arrows.ts) are adapted from mtg-table's
web/src/render/StackPanel.tsx and web/src/render/arrows.ts.
The drafting AI in src/draft/ (rng.ts, weights.ts, pick.ts, draft.ts, and the
card model in cards.ts) is ported from mtg-table's cube lab, tools/cubelab/
(rng.ts, weights.ts, pick.ts, draft.ts, cards.ts): the seeded generator, the
pick scorer and the Grid and Winston rules, stepped one decision at a time.


