3. Scryfall (card data and card images)
---------------------------------------

    Site:     https://scryfall.com
    API docs: https://scryfall.com/docs/api

Card text and card images are fetched from the Scryfall API and
cards.scryfall.io by the user's browser and cached locally in that browser.
They are used under Scryfall's API terms: requests are rate-limited and batched
(/cards/collection), results are cached so they are not re-requested, card
images are shown unaltered with their artist credit and copyright intact, and
ForgeCoach does not proxy, repackage, sell or paywall Scryfall data or imply
Scryfall's endorsement. ForgeCoach is not affiliated with Scryfall.
For the test suite only, src/cube/testdata/scryfall-*.json hold a trimmed
snapshot (name, cost, type, oracle text, colours, produced mana, P/T) of the
cards of the cubes in public/cubes/, so the deck-assistant tests run
offline; the app itself fetches card data live as described above.
The coach benchmark (bench/coach/) likewise keeps a trimmed snapshot of the
card text its cases need in bench/coach/cards.json (name, cost, type, oracle
text, colours, produced mana, P/T, rarity; no images), fetched once from the
Scryfall API so the benchmark builds the same prompts offline.

The cube documents in public/cubes/*.md are Justin's (the project owner's)
cube designs, except public/cubes/evybaby-cube-360.md, Evybaby's New Cube:
Evan's cube (a friend of Justin's): his own 360-card list as he gave it,
here so the two of them can draft it together; and public/cubes/
counter-blitz-fic.md, the decklist of Wizards of the Coast's Final Fantasy X
Commander deck "Counter Blitz" (Final Fantasy Commander, 2025), as Wizards
published it and MTGJSON carries it, a deck Justin owns. Magic: The Gathering
and its card names are Wizards of the Coast's; Final Fantasy is Square Enix's.
The public/cubes/*.meta.json
files are output of mtg-table's cube lab (simulated Forge AI drafts and games).


3a. 17Lands (human card performance data)
-----------------------------------------

    Site:     https://www.17lands.com/public_datasets
    Licence:  Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
              https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

public/cubes/vintage-cube-180.human.json and synergy-cube-180.human.json are
derived from 17Lands' public game data for MTG Arena's Powered Cube
(game_data_public.Cube_-_Powered.PremierDraft.csv.gz and .TradDraft.csv.gz,
"Last Updated" 2025-11-23 on 17Lands' public datasets page). Changes made:
per-card games and wins were aggregated (games with the card in hand, in the
opening hand, and in the deck but never seen), cards were matched to each cube
document (Vintage, Synergy) by name, and cards with fewer than 500 games in
hand were left out; no per-game or per-player data is kept. The lab-number
reliability table in src/cube/labTrust.ts is computed from the Vintage file.
Generator: scripts/human-cards/. The app credits 17Lands, with links to the
dataset page and the licence, wherever the numbers are shown. 17Lands does not
endorse ForgeCoach or its use of the data.

The files public/cubes/*.picks.json are adapted from 17Lands' public draft
data for MTG Arena's Powered Cube (draft_data_public.Cube_-_Powered.
PremierDraft.csv.gz and .TradDraft.csv.gz, last modified 2025-12-01; same
licence). Changes made: a pick model (per-card pick strength and pool-context
coefficients) was fitted to the picks, see docs/human-picks.md, and matched to
each cube document by name; no per-pick, per-draft or per-player data is kept.
Scripts: scripts/human-picks/. The app credits 17Lands, with links to the
dataset page and the licence, wherever the pick signal is shown.


