5. Claude
---------

Coaching text is generated by Anthropic's Claude through the Anthropic API,
using the user's own API key, or by the user pasting a prompt into a Claude app.
ForgeCoach is not affiliated with or endorsed by Anthropic.

Play-mode code adapted from mtg-table
-------------------------------------
src/play/* and src/ui/play/* (the seat session, act builders, the ask dialog
model) adapt behaviour and code from mtg-table's web/src (transport/ws.ts,
render/AskModal.tsx, render/picker.ts, keys.ts, render/PhaseStrip.tsx,
render/labels.ts, render/LogDrawer.tsx, render/describe.ts), GPL-3.0-or-later,
with their copyright lines kept. The phase strip (src/ui/play/PhaseStrip.tsx,
phaseStrip.ts), the log drawer (src/ui/play/LogDrawer.tsx) and the game log's
choice of events (src/eventLog.ts) follow those files. src/ui/play/askFixtures.json and src/play/testdata/ hold
asks and frames recorded by mtg-table's fixture corpus.

The coach benchmark's game logs (bench/coach/logs/*.jsonl.gz) are recordings
from mtg-table's fixture corpus (fixtures/games/human-auto-2026, human-auto-7,
human-number-7, human-scry-7, human-sideboard-7, human-trample-7 and
human-yield-13), gzipped and otherwise unchanged; its cases also use the
public/samples/ and src/play/testdata/ recordings above.

